We will need to know the values of $h(5)$ and $h(8)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
h(5)&=\dfrac{1}{10-5}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{5}
\\\\\\
h(8)&=\dfrac{1}{10-8}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{2}
\\\\\\
\dfrac{h(8)-h(5)}{8-5}&=\dfrac{\dfrac{1}{2}-\dfrac{1}{5}}{3}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{3}{10}\right)}{3}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{10}
\end{align}$
